# Phase 163: the night plan for planets and stars, planned and run.
#
# Kochab and Pherkad are ticked on the Tonight tab, with a globular
# cluster that the plan must list and leave out. PLAN TONIGHT places
# each star in its GOOD or PRIME time; RUN TONIGHT then takes them in
# turn: GoTo (which loads the star's profile), PLANET LOCK's full
# acquisition, and one run of the RUNS sequence.
#
# From the real site (about 33 N) these two stars are in GOOD for only a
# couple of hours a day. At 65 N both stay above 45 deg all day, and each
# is in PRIME about half of it. The emulator's sky follows the rig's site.
# The plan covers the next hour only (NightPlanHours=1), so it never
# waits hours for PRIME: both visits fit in the hour whatever the time.
# Which star goes first depends on the hour, so the steps below do not
# name one.
#
# Centring can take up to about 5 minutes in the afternoon (see
# acquire-runs.scn), so the lock waits 300 s and each visit is 15 min.

name    Night plan: two stars, planned and run
timeout 3600
rig     SiteLatDeg=65
rig     AutorunRuns=1
rig     AutorunGapSec=10
rig     AutorunRefocusEvery=0
rig     AutorunSeeingPct=0
rig     AutorunMinAltDeg=10
rig     NightPlanHours=1
rig     NightPlanVisitMin=15
rig     NightPlanMinVisitMin=3
rig     NightPlanSlewSec=30
rig     NightPlanLockSec=300
rig     NightPlanFocusSec=0

profile star.ini focuser position=168000

expect 30  [SCENARIO] Night plan
wait   3
press  GOTO:TONIGHT
wait   2
press  GOTO:TICK Kochab
expect 10  [NIGHTPLAN] ticked Kochab: 1 ticked
press  GOTO:TICK Pherkad
expect 10  [NIGHTPLAN] ticked Pherkad: 2 ticked
press  GOTO:TICK M13 Hercules Cluster
expect 10  [NIGHTPLAN] ticked M13 Hercules Cluster: 3 ticked
press  GOTO:TICK No Such Star
expect 10  [NIGHTPLAN] TICK refused: no object called 'No Such Star'

# A run with no plan is refused, and says why.
press  GOTO:RUN TONIGHT
expect 10  [NIGHTPLAN] RUN refused: no plan: press PLAN TONIGHT first

press  GOTO:PLAN TONIGHT
expect 30  [NIGHTPLAN] planned 2 visits, 1 skipped
expect 5   [NIGHTPLAN] visit 1:
expect 5   [NIGHTPLAN] visit 2:
expect 5   [NIGHTPLAN] not planned: M13 Hercules Cluster: not a planet or a star
absent 3   [NIGHTPLAN] not planned: Kochab
absent 3   [NIGHTPLAN] not planned: Pherkad
shot   plan-made

press  GOTO:RUN TONIGHT
expect 10  [NIGHTPLAN] running: 2 visits, lock limit 300 s
expect 10  [BUTTON] RUN TONIGHT -> STOP TONIGHT
# At once when the first star is where the plan wants it; otherwise at its
# slot, which is inside the hour.
expect 1200 (1 of 2): slewing
expect 120 SEARCHING
expect 60  : locking
expect 330 : locked, starting the runs
expect 10  [AUTORUN] start: 1 runs
expect 600 [AUTORUN] end:
expect 20  visited: its runs are done
shot   first-done

expect 1500 (2 of 2): slewing
expect 60  : locking
expect 330 : locked, starting the runs
expect 10  [AUTORUN] start: 1 runs
expect 600 [AUTORUN] end:
expect 20  visited: its runs are done
expect 20  [NIGHTPLAN] plan finished: 2 visited, 0 skipped
expect 10  [NOTICE] Night plan finished
expect 10  [BUTTON] STOP TONIGHT -> RUN TONIGHT
absent 3   skipped:
shot   plan-done
